"},{"path":"README.md","action":"add","content":"# Target Tap

Target Tap is a single-player, client-side browser game. Start a 30-second round, tap the target wherever it appears to score points, and see your final score when time runs out.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 20.11 or later (used to run the automated test suite, which relies on the Node test runner's built-in timer mocking)
- Any current desktop browser (Chromium, Firefox, or Safari) to play the game

## Setup

```
npm ci
```

No other setup is required. The application has no runtime dependencies and needs no external service.

## Run

Target Tap is a static, dependency-free application with no server component. Open `index.html` directly in a browser to play it:

```
npm start
```

`npm start` only prints a reminder of this; it does not start a server. You can also open `index.html` directly from a file browser or via `File > Open` in your browser.

## Build

```
npm run build
```

There is no bundling or compilation step. `index.html`, `src/*.js`, and `src/styles.css` are already the deployable artifacts; the `build` script exists to satisfy tooling that expects the command and confirms there is nothing further to produce.

## Test

```
npm test
```

Runs the full automated suite (game state, placement, timer, controller, view, and end-to-end round tests) with Node's built-in test runner.

## Lint

```
npm run lint
```

Checks every source and test file with `node --check`. The project ships with zero dependencies, so this substitutes for an installed linter while still catching syntax errors.

## Scope

This delivery implements only the Must-priority baseline described in `docs/features/simple-game/spec.md` and `docs/features/simple-game/design.md`: starting a round, scoring by hitting a relocating target, a 30-second countdown, a Game Over state with the final score, and restarting via Play Again.

The following are explicitly out of scope for this delivery:

- The Should-priority hit-feedback animation (FR-11)
- The Could-priority session best-score tracking (FR-12)
- The full future feature backlog: difficulty presets, moving targets, combo scoring, miss penalties, best-score persistence, themes, sound and haptics, pause/resume, challenge modes, telemetry, a leaderboard service, and automated replay (F-01 through F-12)

## Known limitations

None known within the baseline scope described above.
